# Both Dockerfile.api and Dockerfile.web build with `context: .` (the repo root,
# see docker-compose.yml) and then COPY only the specific paths they need -- so
# this file is not what keeps unwanted files out of the final images. It exists
# for one load-bearing reason and one speed reason:
#
# Load-bearing: Dockerfile.web runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` for a Linux
# target *inside* the build stage, then `COPY apps/web ./`. Without excluding
# node_modules here, that second COPY would pull in whatever apps/web/node_modules
# already exists on the machine running `docker build` (e.g. this repo, right now,
# has one from local development) and overwrite the freshly-installed Linux one
# with it. On a Mac or with a different pnpm store, that silently breaks the build
# on native-binary packages (esbuild, rollup, lightningcss, ...) with the wrong
# platform underneath -- confirmed by building without this exclusion first.
#
# Speed: everything else here just shrinks what gets sent to the Docker daemon as
# build context (uv/pnpm caches, virtualenvs, git history, other apps' local caches).

.git
.env
.env.local

# Python
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# Node (see "Load-bearing" above)
**/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/.tanstack/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor / tooling noise not needed inside any image
.superpowers/
.claude/
docs/
